 Hardware Components

## Bill of Materials

| # | Component | Purpose |
|---|-----------|---------|
| 1 | Arduino Uno R3 (ATmega328P) | Central processing unit |
| 2 | Piezoelectric Sensor (35mm PZT disc) | Impact/collision detection |
| 3 | MPU6050 (Accelerometer + Gyroscope) | Motion/orientation sensing, sensor fusion |
| 4 | NEO-6M GPS Module | Location acquisition |
| 5 | SIM800L GSM Module | Emergency SMS transmission |
| 6 | Force-Sensitive Resistor (FSR) | Helmet-wear detection |
| 7 | Push Button | Cancel/confirm accident alert |
| 8 | Buzzer | Audible alerts / countdown warning |
| 9 | 2x 18650 Li-ion Cells | Power source (7.4V nominal, in series) |
| 10 | TP4056 Charging Module | Battery charging + protection |
| 11 | 7805 Linear Voltage Regulator | Regulates 7.4V → 5V (Arduino, sensors, GPS) |
| 12 | LM2596 Buck Converter | Regulates 7.4V → 4.0V (GSM module) |

## Key Specifications

**Arduino Uno R3** — ATmega328P, 5V logic, 14 digital I/O (6 PWM), 6 analog in, 16MHz clock, 32KB flash.

**Piezoelectric Sensor** — PZT ceramic, 35mm diameter, 0.5mm thick, 15nF capacitance, charge coefficient 280 pC/N, output 0–5V (with conditioning circuit).

**MPU6050** — 6-axis (3-axis accel + 3-axis gyro), I2C @ 400kHz, 16-bit ADC, 3.3V onboard regulator.

**NEO-6M GPS** — u-blox 6 engine, 2.5m horizontal accuracy, up to 5Hz update rate, UART @ 9600 baud, ~27s cold-start acquisition.

**SIM800L GSM** — Quad-band 850/900/1800/1900 MHz, UART, 3.4–4.4V (recommended 4.0V), up to 350mA peak transmit current.

**FSR** — 12.7mm active area, 0.1N–100N sensitivity range, used with 10kΩ pull-up voltage divider.

## Wiring / Pin Connections

| Module | Signal | Arduino Pin | Interface Type |
|--------|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| Piezo Sensor | Analog Output | A2 | Analog Input |
| Limit Switch (helmet-worn) | Digital | A1 / D2 | Digital Input |
| Push Button (cancel) | Digital | A3 | Digital Input (pull-up) |
| Voice/Mic Module | Analog + Digital | A1 (analog) / D4 (digital) | Analog + Digital Input |
| Buzzer | Alert Output | D5 | Digital Output |
| NEO-6M GPS | RX/TX | D3/D4 (SoftwareSerial) | SoftwareSerial |
| SIM800L GSM | RX/TX | D8/D9 (SoftwareSerial) | SoftwareSerial |
| MPU6050 | SDA/SCL | A4/A5 | I2C |

> Note: pin numbers above reflect the actual firmware (`firmware/smart_helmet.ino`); a couple of pin
> assignments differ slightly from early design tables in the thesis (e.g. GPS/GSM pins were
> reassigned during implementation) — the `.ino` file is the source of truth for wiring.

## Power Supply Circuit

- 2x 18650 Li-ion cells in series → 7.4V nominal
- TP4056 module manages charging from 5V micro-USB input, with battery protection
- 7805 linear regulator: 7.4V → 5V for Arduino, sensors, GPS
- LM2596 buck converter: 7.4V → 4.0V for GSM module (needs stable voltage in its narrow operating range)

## Detection Thresholds (from calibration testing)

- Piezoelectric force threshold: ~15N (also see `VIB_THRESHOLD` in firmware)
- Acceleration magnitude threshold: ~3g
- Verified force detection range in testing: 4.9N – 64.8N
- Detection accuracy achieved: 95%

Full derivation and testing tables are in `docs/thesis.pdf` (Chapters 4–6).
